From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: USA-RedDragon <USA-RedDragon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:12:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(tui-gateway): a chat's slow request no longer holds the
 rest of its socket

A WebSocket answered its frames one at a time in arrival order. A prompt.submit waiting for its
chat's mutation lock (a turn-start claim, a model switch, a held SQLite writer) left every later
frame on the socket unanswered, so on a socket that carries many chats session.list and every
other chat's request timed out behind it.

A frame naming a chat (params.session_id) now dispatches on that chat's own lane, in arrival order
with the chat's other frames. Frames without a chat keep the serial lane, and a chat frame starts
only after the serial frames read before it finished, so connection state a client sets first is in
place for it. Waiting chat frames are bounded; past the bound the reader parks as before. Frames
read before a hang-up still finish before the teardown, a server shutdown cancels them, and after a
reply cannot be sent a lane's unstarted frames are dropped.
